  "authoredFrom": "The relay's delivery (apps/relay/src/deliver.ts) and @superjackfruitlabs/treaty-cloudevents' signDelivery, applied to SuperPipeline's direct push (docs/2026-11-23-every-crossing-phase-2.md, rulings 1 and 2). Every secret is fake. Each body is a valid example from fixtures/superpipeline-events/examples.json, serialised as JSON.stringify writes it.",
  "howToRead": {
    "deliveries": "One delivery from SuperPipeline's direct push to a push config, in CloudEvents HTTP binary mode. `secret` is the config's token; `t` is the second it was signed. Encoding `event` with `http.body` as its data must give exactly `http.headers` without `x-treaty-signature`. Signing `http.body`'s UTF-8 bytes under `event.attributes.id` with `secret` at `t` must give exactly `x-treaty-signature`, which is `t=<t>,v1=<hex HMAC-SHA256 of \"<t>.<id>.<body>\">`. Verifying it must pass at `t` and at `t + toleranceSeconds`. `data` names the example the body is, and the body must validate against the schema `ce-dataschema` names.",
    "refuse": "Verifying `http.headers['x-treaty-signature']` against `http.body` and `http.headers['ce-id']` with `secret`, at `nowSeconds`, must fail. `why` says what is wrong."
  },
  "toleranceSeconds": 300,
